meta {
	name: SameResourceRequestWhilePending
	seq: 99
}

auth {
	mode: inherit
}

docs {
	Scenario: The service owner creates the same resource request again after the requester confirmed it (#5028)

		Given the requester has no open request for the resource
		And the service owner creates a resource request for the requester
		And the requester confirms it, so it is Pending
		When the service owner creates the same resource request again
		Then no new request is created
		And the requester has exactly one open request for the resource, the pending one
		Finally the requester withdraws the open requests to clean up

	Today the check for an existing request only looks at drafts, so a new draft is created
	beside the pending request, and the party can be asked twice.

	## Expected behaviour

	The issue asks for duplicates to be prevented, not for a particular response. The WHEN step
	accepts either 202 with the pending request that already exists, or 409, and fails on 202
	with a new request. Narrow it once the fix settles on one response.

	## Run order

	`seq: 99` runs this scenario after the other steps in this folder. Its GIVEN and CLEANUP
	steps withdraw every open request from the requester for the resource, including what the steps
	above may leave pending.

	## Environments and the fix

	Every step starts with `skipOutsideEnabledEnvironments()` from
	`utils/serviceOwnerRequestWhilePending.js`: `enabledEnvironments` lists where the personas are
	verified, `fixedEnvironments` where the fix for #5028 is deployed. The scenario runs only where
	both apply, so the post-deployment run stays green until the fix is out.

	## Tokens and fixtures

	Personas live in `testdata/delegationrequest-scenarios/<tokenEnv>.js` under
	`serviceOwnerRequestWhilePending`. The service owner steps use a Maskinporten enterprise token
	for ttd with `altinn:serviceowner/delegationrequests.write`, the requester steps a personal
	token with `altinn:portal/enduser`.
}
